data.content:
**Yes, C# fully supports `stackalloc` into a `Span` of native-sized integers.** Both `Span<nint>` and `Span<nuint>` work:

```csharp
Span<nint> span = stackalloc nint[5];
Span<nuint> uspan = stackalloc nuint[3];
```

On this 64-bit system, `nint.Size` is 8 bytes and `nuint.MaxValue` is `18446744073709551615` (2⁶⁴−1). This has been supported since C# 9 / .NET 5, when `nint`/`nuint` were introduced as first-class unmanaged types (which is the requirement for `stackalloc`).
